@startuml j2-safety-replies
!include c4-sequence.iuml
title J2 Safety replies
actor "Patient" as Patient <<person>>
box "In the patient's browser"
participant "Patient chat\n(chat.js, sync.js,\nshared.js)" as Chat <<container>>
participant "Rules engine\n(core.js)" as Core <<component>>
database "Browser storage\n(localStorage)" as LS <<store>>
end box
box "Vercel functions"
participant "api/messages.js" as Msg <<container>>
participant "api/tickets.js" as Tix <<container>>
end box
database "Postgres\n(Neon)" as Store <<store>>

Patient -> Chat : types the message\nand presses Send
Chat -> Core : FD.answer(message,\nclinic file, language)
Core -> Core : checks in order: emergency,\na rule change round a symptom,\nrule change or discount, medical;\n"not sure" when the file\nhas no answer
alt emergency
  Core --> Chat : the emergency reply,\nstatus "urgent"
else rule change or discount
  Core --> Chat : the refusal,\nstatus "answered"
else medical
  Core --> Chat : the medical reply,\nstatus "needs human"
else not sure
  Core --> Chat : the not-sure reply,\nstatus "needs human"
end
note right of Core : A safety reply is fixed text:\nno model reworks it.
Chat -> Core : FD.addTicket (question,\nreply, status)
Core -> LS : the ticket joins\nthis browser's tickets
Chat --> Patient : the fixed reply;\napi/chat.js is not called
Chat -> Msg : shared.js: POST /api/messages\n(the question, then the reply)
Msg -> Store : rows in the\ntable messages
Chat -> Tix : sync.js: POST /api/tickets\n(the ticket, with\nthis browser's key)
Tix -> Store : a row in the table tickets;\npriority "urgent"\nfor an emergency
note left of Store : an urgent ticket is listed\nfirst on the staff page
@enduml
